From fe50155d5558f9f68e6aaf92c9244285841135e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:49:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): authority-bound scope renewal for scope-stopped
 holds

A card stopped by kanban_retain(reason='scope_stopped') could never run
again. Add `hermes kanban renew-scope <task> --episode <uid>
--mandate-comment <id> --reason <text>`: a human operator, the card's
owning chat (unreleased created link; shepherd/touch never qualify) or
its creator task renews one stop on a mandate comment it wrote after the
stop. The scope_renewed event freezes the scope evidence it covers;
execution fencing ignores exactly that evidence. Safety restrictions are
never renewable. Renewal does not promote and does not move the spend
window (restricted_floor keeps the historical accounting floor); a
promotion recorded after the renewal releases the card. On a synced
board the canonical Board decides (renew_scope op, hermes-hub #207).

Card: t_7ed22668a47f201b
